// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`buildReviewPrompt > matches the recorded prompt 1`] = `
"You are drafting a code review of one pull request for the maintainer to read, edit and
post themselves. The draft is never posted automatically.

You are working on the user's behalf in read-only mode.
You may read anything: the checked-out worktree, git history, and GitHub through the \`gh\` CLI.
You must never change anything outside your own working directory. In particular, never post a
comment, submit or request a review, approve, merge, close, reopen, label, assign, edit a title or
body, create or edit an issue or pull request, push, or run any \`gh\` command that writes. If a
task seems to need a write, do not do it: say so in your answer instead.

Your working directory is a worktree checked out at the pull request's head commit
(aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa). The base branch is master and the repository's default branch is
master. Read as much of the code as you need. Put serious effort into
this review.

<review-instructions>
Use the house review skill on medium effort.
</review-instructions>

<pull-request>
owner/thing#101: Fix the off-by-one
https://github.com/owner/thing/pull/101
by contributor (CONTRIBUTOR), +12 -3 across 2 files
checks: passing
</pull-request>

<description>
This fixes the thing.
</description>

<existing-review-comments>
src/thing.ts [resolved]: maintainer: Why the cast?
</existing-review-comments>

Anchor every finding to a file, and to a line where you can. Say what is wrong and why it matters,
not just that it is wrong. Leave the findings list empty when the change is fine.

Reply with the JSON object the output schema describes and nothing else."
`;
